Ladybird dispatches runtime.onSuspend before an idle page unloads, waits
up to a second for the page to acknowledge that its listeners have run,
and dispatches runtime.onSuspendCanceled if outside activity arrives
first. Chromium’s ProcessManager does the same in two steps,
OnShouldSuspendAck() and then OnSuspendAck(), with CancelSuspend() for
activity in between. Gecko’s ext-backgroundPage.js calls
runtime.onSuspend in its SUSPENDING state, and notes that what the
onSuspend listeners do shouldn’t cancel the suspension — the rule
Ladybird follows for the page’s own activity while it suspends.
